If asynchronous → those 5 go into an internal retry queue

🔹 2. Queuing
Queuing happens when the event source itself is a queueing service (like SQS or SNS).

If Lambda is at max concurrency, the unprocessed messages just wait in the queue until Lambda has capacity to pick them.

No request is lost unless the message expires (e.g., SQS visibility timeout or retention period ends).

📌 Example:

Lambda connected to SQS

10,000 messages arrive in queue

Lambda concurrency = 500

Lambda pulls 500 messages, processes them

Remaining 9,500 stay in the queue until capacity frees up

🔹 Simple Real-Life Analogy
